.parquet

This template reads an s3:// parquet address in `_file` itself (D1486):
the page signs it (fused.s3.sign), passes the HTTPS URL to reader.py, and
DuckDB reads it with its httpfs extension, so a page reads the footer and the row groups and columns it
shows, never the whole object. Only parquet streams: CSV/JSON have no footer
to page from. Lines starting with "." list the extensions it streams.
